.TH XUR.STD.STUB.IL2CPP 7 "2026-10-30" "xur 0.1.2" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.stub.il2cpp \- interact with a live Unity Il2Cpp game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B use std::stub::il2cpp;
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::stub::il2cpp
provides runtime access to a Unity Il2Cpp game's types, fields,
methods, and objects from inside the injected process. It is the
primary module for writing game mods and trainers.
.PP
Fields can be read/written, methods can be invoked, and methods can
be hooked with closures that intercept calls at runtime.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B loaded() -> Result<Runtime>
Get the Il2Cpp runtime handle. Fails if Il2Cpp has not initialised yet.
.TP
.B null() -> Object
Return a null managed object reference.
.SH Runtime METHODS
.TP
.B class(assembly, namespace, name) -> Result<Class>
Look up a managed class by assembly name, namespace, and class name.
.TP
.B string(value) -> Object
Create a managed System.String from a xur string.
.TP
.B assemblies() -> [Image]
List all loaded assemblies as Image objects.
.SH Class METHODS
.TP
.B field(name) -> Result<Field>
Look up a field by name.
.TP
.B method(name, param_count) -> Result<Method>
Look up a method by name and parameter count.
.TP
.B new_object() -> Object
Allocate a new managed object of this class (does not call a constructor).
.TP
.B fields() -> [Field]
List all fields on the class.
.TP
.B methods() -> [Method]
List all methods on the class.
.TP
.B name() -> str
The class name.
.TP
.B namespace() -> str
The class namespace.
.SH Field METHODS
.TP
.B read(object) -> value
Read this instance field's value from an object. The return type depends
on the field's element type (bool, int, float, or Object).
.TP
.B write(object, value) -> ()
Write a value to this instance field on an object.
.TP
.B read_static() -> value
Read a static field's value.
.TP
.B write_static(value) -> ()
Write a value to a static field.
.TP
.B name() -> str
The field name.
.TP
.B type_name() -> str
The field's type name.
.TP
.B offset() -> int
The field's offset in the object layout.
.TP
.B is_static() -> bool
Whether the field is static.
.SH Method METHODS
.TP
.B invoke(object, args...) -> value
Call the method via il2cpp_runtime_invoke. The first argument after the
method is the instance object (or
.BR null() ).
Remaining arguments are boxed and passed to the method.
.TP
.B invoke_on_main(object, args...) -> value
Like
.B invoke
but dispatches the call to Unity's main thread and blocks until it
completes. Use this for methods that instantiate GameObjects or fire
events that touch the Unity API, which is only safe from the main
thread. The call executes on the next frame's update and the result is
returned to the caller.
.TP
.B hook(callback) -> ()
Install a generic hook on this method. The callback receives a
.B HookContext
and returns
.B Option<value>
\(em
.B None
passes through to the original,
.B Some(value)
overrides the return value.
.TP
.B hook_void_block() -> VoidBlockHook
Install a simple block/unblock hook. When blocked, the method returns
immediately without executing. Useful for void methods where you just
want to prevent execution.
.TP
.B name() -> str
The method name.
.TP
.B signature() -> str
The full method signature string.
.TP
.B code_address() -> int
The native code address of the method.
.SH HookContext METHODS
Available inside a
.BR hook() " callback:"
.TP
.B arg(index_or_name) -> value
Read a marshalled argument by index (int) or parameter name (str).
.TP
.B args() -> [value]
All marshalled arguments as a list.
.TP
.B set_arg(index_or_name, value) -> ()
Mark an argument as modified. Changes are written back to the
saved registers before the original is called.
.TP
.B signature() -> str
The hooked method's signature string.
.TP
.B call() -> value
Call the original method with the (possibly modified) arguments.
Can only be called once per hook invocation. Returns the original's
return value.
.SH VoidBlockHook METHODS
.TP
.B set_blocked(blocked: bool) -> ()
Enable or disable blocking.
.TP
.B is_blocked() -> bool
Whether the hook is currently blocking.
.SH Image METHODS
.TP
.B name() -> str
The assembly image name.
.TP
.B classes() -> [Class]
All classes in this assembly image.
.SH IL2CPP PROXY MACROS
The
.B #[il2cpp_proxy]
attribute macro generates constructors for structs that map to IL2CPP
classes, eliminating manual class/field/method lookup boilerplate.
.SS Struct Attributes
.TP
.B #[il2cpp_proxy(asm="A", ns="N", class="C")]
Marks a struct as a proxy for the IL2CPP class
.I C
in namespace
.I N
of assembly
.IR A .
The
.I ns
argument defaults to "" if omitted.
Generates
.B from_runtime(rt)
and
.B from_class(cls)
constructors.
.SS Field Attributes
.TP
.B #[il2cpp_field="name"]
The field stores an
.B il2cpp::Field
looked up as
.BR cls.field("name") .
If the value form is used, the IL2CPP name matches the value. Otherwise
.BR #[il2cpp_field(name="N")] " or " #[il2cpp_field(name="N", static)]
can be used.
.TP
.B #[il2cpp_method(name="N", params=P)]
The field stores an
.B il2cpp::Method
looked up as
.BR cls.method("N",\ P) .
.TP
.B #[il2cpp_hook(name="N")]
The field stores an
.B il2cpp::VoidBlockHook
created by
.BR cls.method("N",\ P)?.hook_void_block() .
.SS Impl Block Expansion
.B #[il2cpp_proxy]
on an impl block generates a
.B setup_hooks()
method. Functions annotated with
.B #[il2cpp_hook(method="field")]
are wired up as
.BR self.field.hook(Self::fn) .
.SS Hook Data
Extra parameters beyond
.B ctx
on a hook function are treated as shared state.
The expander generates a
.B Type::default()
call for each, wraps the hook in a closure that passes them through, and
returns a record from
.B setup_hooks()
so the caller can read and write the data at runtime.
.PP
The data type must have a static
.B default()
function (conventionally marked with
.BR #[default] )
that returns an instance. Fields using
.B cell::Cell
share identity through
.B Arc
when captured, so both the hook closure and the returned record see the
same mutable state.
.PP
.nf
struct HookState {
    godmode: cell::Cell<bool>
}
impl HookState {
    #[default]
    fn default() -> HookState {
        HookState { godmode: cell::new(false) }
    }
}

#[il2cpp_proxy]
impl HealthProxy {
    #[il2cpp_hook(method="damage")]
    fn on_damage(ctx: il2cpp::HookContext, state: HookState) -> _ {
        if state.godmode.get() { Some(0) } else { None }
    }
}

let hooks = proxy.setup_hooks();
hooks.state.godmode.set(true);
.fi
.SS Scoped Import
The macro lives in the
.B std::stub::il2cpp
module. Import it before use:
.PP
.nf
use std::stub::il2cpp::il2cpp_proxy;
.fi
.PP
Or use the full path directly:
.B #[std::stub::il2cpp::il2cpp_proxy(...)]
.SS Example
.nf
use std::stub::il2cpp::il2cpp_proxy;

#[il2cpp_proxy(asm="Assembly-CSharp", ns="", class="PlayerHealth")]
struct HealthProxy {
    #[il2cpp_field="hp"]
    hp: il2cpp::Field
    #[il2cpp_field="maxHp"]
    max_hp: il2cpp::Field
    #[il2cpp_method(name="DamagePlayer", params=3)]
    damage: il2cpp::Method
}

fn main() -> Result<()> {
    let rt = il2cpp::loaded()?;
    let proxy = HealthProxy::from_runtime(rt)?;
    // proxy.hp, proxy.damage etc. are ready to use
    Ok(())
}
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::stub::il2cpp;
use std::log;

fn ctor() {
    log::subscriber().to_file("/tmp/mod.log").init();
}

fn stub_main() {
    let rt = il2cpp::loaded().unwrap();
    let cls = rt.class("Assembly-CSharp", "", "PlayerHealth").unwrap();
    let hp = cls.field("hp").unwrap();
    let damage = cls.method("DamagePlayer", 3).unwrap();

    // Godmode: intercept damage calls
    damage.hook(|ctx| {
        log::info("blocked damage");
        Some(0)
    });
}
.fi
